    "title": "Testimonials",
    "description": "A quote wall: only approved quotes are public; editors review them in a managed list with approve and hide actions.",
    "tags": [
        "cms-in-cms",
        "list only",
        "moderation",
        "quick actions",
        "translatable"
    ],
    "_comment": "CMS-in-CMS template: a Testimonials wall in two pages (list only). PUBLIC: /testimonials is a read-only data view (cards) of the table of the form \"@section:testimonials-form\"; a fixed filter limits it to approved quotes, so a quote that is pending or hidden never reaches a visitor, whatever the address says. CMS: /cms/testimonials is ONE entry-form-list that holds the form: review the quotes, approve or hide one with a click (quick actions that change the status), add and edit quotes in a dialog, delete them and restore earlier versions. The inputs are defined once, in the form inside the list. data_tables[] carries the columns and sample rows (import with options.importData=true). The quote and the role are translatable. Content locales: de-CH + en-GB. Pages are not open to guests until you set their access. Import via Admin > CMS Apps > Import template. NOT auto-seeded.",
